    Script: log-rotation.d. Existing syslogd probes describe a different stage.

Already instrumented: inspect gaps, do not recreate providers
------------------------------------------------------------
SysV message/semaphore/shared memory, POSIX queues, AIO, pipes and UNIX-domain
sockets have source probes. TCP/SCTP/IPsec use header/statistics wrappers,
so searching only C files undercounts them. FUSE has substantial existing
probe coverage. PAM modules, cron, syslogd and devd have userspace wrappers.
For these, audit unmatched starts, missing cancellation/result fields and
cross-thread correlation before adding another broad provider.

Recommended rollout
-------------------
First implement Priority A with explicit pair/result contracts and matching
profiles, then Priority B in coherent library/service groups. Keep each
subsystem's live workloads and uncovered paths in its inventory. The 61-probe
batch preceding this audit remains a baseline, with its exact stage limits
in KERNEL-PROBES-NEXT; it does not fully instrument every operation in those
14 subsystems. Maximum practical coverage is measured by observable lifecycles
and branch outcomes, not the total number of declarations.
